<title>UK: Warner Village plans huge cinema by Thames.</title>
<headline>Warner Village plans huge cinema by Thames.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Warner Village Cinemas on Monday announced plans to build what it called the world's largest multi-screen cinema complex at the disused Battersea power station, a landmark site on the south bank of the Thames in London.</p>
<p>The joint venture between Warner Brothers International and the Australia-based Village Roadshow Ltd will include a 32-screen theatre seating over 8,200 people.</p>
<p>&quot;We are delighted to have secured Warner Village cinemas as a key partner for this exciting project,&quot; Victor Hwang of Parkview International which owns the site said in a statement.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
